KG42.register("clusters-21fac8822f42b62b827d2312",{"id":"29-smart_home_trading::v142-d-CL001","paper":"29-smart_home_trading","label":"Alternating pricing, energy allocation, and per-household cost protection in centralized microgrid trading","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Alternating pricing, energy allocation, and per-household cost protection in centralized microgrid trading","market_meaning":"In an already formed microgrid with P2P trading capability, a central processing center collects and processes household information; when trading quantities are fixed, Module 2 selects the microgrid price by combining the total cost objective, price bounds, and per-household cost protection, and Module 3 then calculates, at the fixed price, the energy allocation satisfying household balance, microgrid revenue-expenditure balance, and trading bounds. The commodity chain clarifies the traded energy and the buy/sell sign convention. The existing chain supports this alternating-optimization candidate, but initialization, the complete feasible region, and termination closure still have gaps.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","pricing","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Each chain belongs to the same ECO-Trade microgrid algorithm, but the variable and parameter roles of Module 2 and Module 3 must be kept separate; the first round uses Module 1's DS, and only subsequently does Module 3's ME get fed back. The clearing-stage label of R002 and the pricing label of R006 are retained according to the original chains. The central processing responsibility only provides the architectural scope, and the commodity definition only unifies the convention for the traded object; price units and model closure issues remain unresolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Assembled according to the explicit price and trading-quantity interface, cost definitions, and shared cost-protection within the same algorithm, and incorporating the central processing responsibility and commodity definition that support this calculation. The boundary is not determined by shared nodes; the trading time limit in the no-storage case and the optional aggregator delegation in the introduction are retained as independent clusters.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertakes energy allocation under fixed prices, household and microgrid balance, trading bounds, and per-household cost protection."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertakes price selection under fixed trading quantities, price bounds, and the feedback interface with energy allocation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements total cost and household cost definitions; the Module 2 objective and cost protection restated in R006 are retained as duplicate expressions of the same model and are not counted as separate rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Limits the algorithm to an architecture that centrally collects and processes household information; no specific message interface or new dependency edge is fabricated on that basis."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Clarifies the traded-energy commodity and buy/sell signs in the allocation and pricing interfaces, without independently expanding execution, pairing, or settlement obligations."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x01"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta.MP_h","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E24"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that Module 2 outputs the price and Module 3 fixes it and then solves for trading quantities; this records the cross-chain quantity interface and existing stage conditions and adds no new C scientific edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x.ME_kh"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th02","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E16"],"rationale":"When iteration continues, the ME obtained by Module 3 serves as a fixed input to the next Module 2. The first price solve uses DS for initialization, and this initial value source cannot be equated with Module 3 feedback."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The two chains restate the same Module 2 total cost objective and per-household cost protection; R002's cost definitions and R006's price bounds and feedback interface are retained separately, and the duplicated parts are not treated as additional market rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x.C_k","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24"],"rationale":"The household cost definition and the condition of being no worse than the no-trading benchmark jointly explain the cost auxiliary quantity and protection constraint in Module 3. The source text states that the Module 3 model is similar to Module 2, but the fixed quantities and feasible regions of the two stages still apply separately, and constraint instances are not merged on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x.ME_kh","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g02-E27"],"rationale":"The signed household traded energy defined by the commodity chain is exactly the microgrid balance object of the allocation chain; this interface adds no counterparty matching or physical execution constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E16"],"rationale":"Central collection and processing of information is the architectural scope of the proposed algorithm, and Module 2 is the pricing stage of that algorithm. This mapping supplements the responsibility background and does not turn architectural narration into a field-by-field dependency relation not given by the source text."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R006::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E24"],"rationale":"Both refer to the local energy allocation function in the same algorithm. Only a display reference is selected; both frozen node references and their local bindings are fully retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E24"],"rationale":"Both refer to the microgrid price calculation function of Module 2; the representative reference is for display only and does not rewrite the edge and constraint attribution of each chain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x.ME_kh","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-ME","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th02","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g02-E26"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that these references correspond to the microgrid traded energy of the same household and time slot, and makes explicit their Module 2 parameter and Module 3 variable roles. Objects for each module and iteration time point are retained separately; values in different rounds are not asserted to be equal, and they are not merged with DS or MQ."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta.MP_h","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-MP","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x01"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E24"],"rationale":"For the same microgrid time-slot price, Module 2 treats it as a variable and Module 3 as a fixed parameter, and this identity is supported by explicit module descriptions. Differences in price units and domain notation are still retained pending verification, and the object is not rewritten on that basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta.CkNoTrade","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-CkNoTrade","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th03"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"All use the no-trading-cost benchmark obtained by Module 1 for the same household and scenario; local parameter references are retained separately, and the benchmark is not mistaken for a cost newly obtained by Module 3."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-GP","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th01"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E22"],"rationale":"Both are grid prices given by time slot in the same Module 2 model. Missing and differing unit metadata are not filled in D."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x.GE_kh","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-GE"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g02-E25"],"rationale":"Both semantically mean the energy that the household obtains from the grid within the time slot; Module 2 and Module 3 solve separately, and semantic association does not equal forcing the values from the two solves to be identical."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM008","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E20"],"rationale":"Both are the Module 2 total cost objective under fixed trading quantities. Only the objective formulation is displayed as one representative; differences in local variable bindings and the cost definitions in R002 are retained, and the model cannot therefore be deemed closed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM009","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"Both restate source constraint (24) of the same Module 2 and the same participating household scope. The protection condition of R001 in price-fixed Module 3 is additionally retained as a stage instance and is not deduplicated together merely because of shared citation."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM010","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29"],"rationale":"The two records share source equation (28) and explain the seller and buyer conditions respectively. The conditions differ, so two explanatory references are retained, no unique representative is selected, and they are not counted as two independent market rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence cited by this cluster remains unverified and supports candidate assembly only under experimental permission; no B source audit, C2 independent review, or Agent E review has been performed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g02-E25","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the cited original text, formulas, and applicable scope, and inspect all assembly mappings; experimental citability must not be interpreted as verified transcription or scientific correctness."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The existing chain does not include Module 2's (21) or the common constraints (4)-(15) required by both modules, and the feasible region for storage dynamics, device scheduling, renewable energy availability, and grid limits is not closed. Module 3's (25) cannot replace Module 2's inequality balance.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R001::x::x.SE_kh","v141-c-R001::x::x.S_kih","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-tau","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream C will supplement the missing stage constraints, objects, and bindings, and clarify which conditions Module 3 inherits; D retains existing content and does not add feasible-region formulations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The initial trading quantities and per-household no-trading-cost benchmarks come from Module 1, but the supplied chain does not include Module 1's complete optimization and output chain; therefore these quantities can only be cited as given inputs, and initialization cannot be reproduced from this cluster.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th04","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th03","v141-c-R001::theta::theta.CkNoTrade","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-CkNoTrade"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g02-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the Module 1 chain and the source explanation from optimization results to DS and cost benchmark parameters; clarify the stage distinction from subsequent Module 3 feedback, and do not calculate values in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The total cost definition does not directly contain the microgrid price, but includes grid energy draw and device end-of-horizon states; the price participates in constraints through per-household costs and price bounds. R006 lists only price decision references and cannot replace the other decisions presented in R002 or the complete Module 2 model, and the existing materials also cannot guarantee price uniqueness.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x01","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the complete decision set and constraint coupling of Module 2, and check whether the source text provides a price-selection method when multiple solutions exist; if not, retain price selection as undetermined and do not claim that the objective directly determines a unique price."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R001 records the microgrid price unit as cent, R006 records the price as cent/kWh, and some relevant units in R002 are empty; B also refers to the price unit collectively as cent. The positive-real notation of the price domain and the price bounds permitting zero also need verification. The current quantity association does not resolve these metadata issues.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta.MP_h","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-MP","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-GP","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x01","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th01"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E41"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original price units, domain conventions, and cost dimensions, and have upstream interpret or revise the metadata; all original objects remain accessible, and D does not automatically convert or unify units."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G006","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R006's existing C2 binding binds Module 1's DS and no-trading-cost benchmark to the same clearing-to-pricing edge, and that edge also carries Module 3 trading-quantity feedback. The frozen nodes do not distinguish these two calculation sources, and it cannot be inferred that Module 3 produces initialization quantities or benchmarks.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th03","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-th04","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should inspect the binding scope of Module 1 inputs and Module 3 feedback; this time the frozen binding is retained, and D only interprets the interface according to the explicit first-round and continuation-round conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G007","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The chain contains only the alternating order and feedback interface, with no complete record of termination calculation and final solution selection. There is a pending verification discrepancy between the B pseudocode's inclusive loop bound and the prose description of consecutive counts, and no handling is given for the relative improvement calculation when the previous cost is zero.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the algorithm control chain and check the counting convention, stopping conditions, final output, and zero-denominator case; this cluster does not choose an interpretation or fabricate control formulas on its own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G008","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The condition that each household is no worse than the no-trading benchmark has a different meaning from the aggregate total cost objective, and clearing.social_welfare cannot replace individual cost protection. Related proposal v141-b-g03-P01 remains pending; this cluster only retains existing constraint references and inserts no new nodes or declares global Pareto optimality.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E14"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually evaluate this pending proposal and the terminology boundary; before any framework extension is confirmed, continue to express per-household protection with the existing constraint and distinguish this condition from a proof of global optimality."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001's (25) and (27) connect load and charging power terms labeled in kW with kWh energy, and the existing chain does not explain the conversion convention for time-slot duration. B's 1h case cannot automatically eliminate the dimensional question under its claim of arbitrary temporal granularity.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R001::theta::theta.p_ki","v141-c-R001::theta::theta.SP_k","v141-c-R001::x::x.ME_kh"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E25","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E41"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the time-slot convention and power/energy conventions implicit in the source text; upstream should supplement applicable conditions or retain an explanation that the dimensions remain unresolved; D does not alter equations or add conversion factors."}]},"rule_refs":["29-smart_home_trading::v141-c-R001","29-smart_home_trading::v141-c-R006","29-smart_home_trading::v141-c-R002","29-smart_home_trading::v141-c-R003","29-smart_home_trading::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-0e667e8e9feb7467","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","COMP-f0015e75a5829a38","KG40-88d16cf517d0bffb","KG40-f19328f0aeb3d626"]});
